WEBVTT

00:00:14.638 --> 00:00:16.389
[helicopter approaching]

00:00:26.692 --> 00:00:28.693
[electricity crackling]

00:00:33.282 --> 00:00:37.118
Now, this is what a true bad guy
looks like.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.079
[helmet whirs]

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:45.710
What do you say we have some fun?

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:52.133
[maniacal laughing]

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:55.637
[laughing continues]

00:00:58.099 --> 00:01:00.225
[screeching]

00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:12.737
[gasping]

00:01:15.032 --> 00:01:17.283
[people screaming]

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:25.834
Hey.

00:01:26.669 --> 00:01:27.669
You okay?

00:01:28.337 --> 00:01:29.546
No, I'm not okay.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:31.881
I'm very, very un-okay.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:36.302
Um, I just left the only friends
I have ever had, so what am...

00:01:37.346 --> 00:01:38.555
What am I doin'?

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:41.057
[sighs]

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.351
I know this isn't easy,

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:45.812
leaving everything behind.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.481
- Do you?
- Yeah.

00:01:48.566 --> 00:01:50.733
I was the best thief in the world.

00:01:50.818 --> 00:01:53.862
Fast, fearless, inventive.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.198
I just had one thing left to steal.

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.284
The Golden Dolphin.

00:01:59.368 --> 00:02:00.410
So you went after it.

00:02:01.495 --> 00:02:02.912
I didn't just go after it.

00:02:04.582 --> 00:02:05.999
<i>I had it.</i>

00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:08.042
<i>And a clear escape route.</i>

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.297
<i>But...</i>

00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:17.760
<i>all I saw in the end was the tricky fox</i>
<i>that they always told me I was.</i>

00:02:20.055 --> 00:02:21.472
<i>It changed everything.</i>

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.352
So, now, instead of hurting people,
I'm helping them.

00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:28.146
I'm still me. [chuckles]

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.316
I'm just me, on the right side.

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:35.153
You're doing the right thing.

00:02:35.237 --> 00:02:37.906
And some day, your friends,
if they're real friends,

00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:40.116
I think they'll understand.

00:02:41.493 --> 00:02:43.411
Now, come on, let's get inside.

00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:45.288
You look like
you just busted out of a prison.

00:02:45.372 --> 00:02:46.372
[chuckling]

00:02:46.457 --> 00:02:47.624
- [thuds]
- [both gasp]

00:02:47.708 --> 00:02:49.459
[guinea pig chittering]

00:02:49.543 --> 00:02:50.835
Guinea pigs?

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.712
- [gasps]
- [both] Marmalade!

00:02:52.796 --> 00:02:53.713
Let's bounce.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:58.301
So, this is the hideout
of the great Crimson Paw.

00:02:58.385 --> 00:02:59.636
- [Diane chuckles]
- [keypad beeping]

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:00.887
Snack break?

00:03:00.971 --> 00:03:03.473
Okay, oddly timed, but you do you.

00:03:03.557 --> 00:03:05.475
- [automated voice] ldentity verified.
- What?

00:03:05.559 --> 00:03:07.018
<i>Welcome, Diane.</i>

00:03:12.816 --> 00:03:14.025
Whoa!

00:03:14.109 --> 00:03:16.569
Holy moly!

00:03:16.654 --> 00:03:18.780
Ah! It's so good to be home.

00:03:18.864 --> 00:03:20.073
Are you kiddin' me?

00:03:20.157 --> 00:03:21.658
Laser-sighted zip line?

00:03:21.742 --> 00:03:24.661
The XM 2400 Radar Jammer? No way!

00:03:24.745 --> 00:03:26.746
I actually prefer the earlier model.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.957
Agree to disagree.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.501
This stuff is nice too. [screams]

00:03:31.585 --> 00:03:33.169
Yeah, that's a blowtorch.

00:03:33.254 --> 00:03:35.004
Also, not really your color.

00:03:35.089 --> 00:03:36.130
Ugh.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:37.382
[Diane] All righty.

00:03:37.466 --> 00:03:42.095
Marmalade, what are you up to,
you fuzzy little weirdo?

00:03:42.179 --> 00:03:43.596
We need eyes on the city.

00:03:43.681 --> 00:03:47.058
Let's see if we can't hack into
the government's surveillance satellite.

00:03:47.142 --> 00:03:48.810
But you're the governor.
Couldn't you just ask?

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:50.436
Yeah, but the paperwork.

00:03:50.521 --> 00:03:52.063
[beeping]

00:03:52.147 --> 00:03:55.650
[Diane mumbling]

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:59.570
I am definitely picking up on
suspicious activity here.

00:03:59.655 --> 00:04:01.781
Those are guinea pig heat signatures.

00:04:01.865 --> 00:04:04.033
Marmalade seems to be
controlling them.

00:04:04.702 --> 00:04:06.202
But to do what?

00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:07.495
There are no obvious targets.

00:04:10.457 --> 00:04:12.166
That's because they're moving targets.

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:14.794
[gasps] His charity fundraiser.

00:04:14.878 --> 00:04:17.797
He's gonna steal the money.
Raised in his own name?

00:04:17.881 --> 00:04:20.341
It's the greatest heist
the world's ever seen.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.677
One billion dollars inside trucks

00:04:22.761 --> 00:04:24.762
on their way to charities
all over the city.

00:04:24.847 --> 00:04:26.306
We need to cut off
Marmalade's communication

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:27.390
with his guinea pig army.

00:04:27.474 --> 00:04:28.975
If there's no signal...

00:04:29.059 --> 00:04:30.310
There's no heist.

00:04:30.394 --> 00:04:32.895
[both] We have to steal the meteorite.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:34.022
That was very cute...

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:35.398
- All right.
- ...what we just did there.

00:04:35.482 --> 00:04:37.817
Put on your big-girl pants.
We're gearin' up.

00:04:44.325 --> 00:04:46.743
I wouldn't take that.
Those things rip your pants right off.

00:04:46.827 --> 00:04:50.163
Huh. Try wearing clean underwear.
Just in case.

00:04:51.373 --> 00:04:52.457
What...

00:04:54.251 --> 00:04:56.127
You stole my car?

00:04:56.211 --> 00:04:57.879
Respect.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:00.173
Let's do this.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.684
- [elevator bell dings]
- [all gasp]

00:05:11.769 --> 00:05:12.810
- [Shark] No!
- [Snake] What?

00:05:12.895 --> 00:05:14.103
[Piranha] All our stuff?

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.356
- [Tarantula] Oh, no.
- Where is everything?

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.649
- No, no, no!
- All our stuff.

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:20.860
- It's all gone!
- My disguise closet!

00:05:20.944 --> 00:05:22.403
[Tarantula]
Where's my things?

00:05:23.781 --> 00:05:26.199
Wolf gave away all our loot!

00:05:26.283 --> 00:05:28.743
We stole it fair and square!

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:32.246
Now I understand what it feels like
to have things stolen from you.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.791
[panting] I don't like it.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:38.753
I really don't like it! [whimpering]

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:45.218
- [grumbles]
- [Shark crying] We got no food.

00:05:45.302 --> 00:05:47.512
We got no money.
We got no money we could use to buy food.

00:05:47.596 --> 00:05:49.097
No food we can sell for money.

00:05:49.723 --> 00:05:52.016
We... [cries]

00:05:52.768 --> 00:05:54.268
All right! Okay, okay.

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:55.978
Here, here. Take it.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.272
Now, stop cryin', buddy.

00:05:58.857 --> 00:06:00.483
Oh!

00:06:02.152 --> 00:06:06.155
Um... Snake, what did you just do?

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.907
What? My friend was sad.

00:06:07.991 --> 00:06:09.534
I was just cheerin' him up.

00:06:09.618 --> 00:06:10.827
You...

00:06:10.911 --> 00:06:12.829
You did a good thing. For me.

00:06:12.913 --> 00:06:13.996
Don't be ridiculous.

00:06:14.081 --> 00:06:16.416
I just put your needs before my own.

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.043
- Yeah. You're being good.
- I'm not.

00:06:19.128 --> 00:06:22.088
I was simply making a sacrifice
so Shark could be happy.

00:06:22.172 --> 00:06:25.007
That is the actual definition
of being good.

00:06:25.092 --> 00:06:26.259
Snake!

00:06:26.343 --> 00:06:28.136
You! The worst one of us!

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.346
- The most selfish.
- Spiteful.

00:06:30.431 --> 00:06:31.556
- Terrible.
- Sneaky.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:32.932
- Dishonest.
- Insensitive.

00:06:33.016 --> 00:06:34.016
- Manipulative.
- Snake-like.

00:06:34.101 --> 00:06:36.269
- Stanky.
- And your point is?

00:06:36.854 --> 00:06:38.729
I think Wolf was right.

00:06:38.814 --> 00:06:41.607
Maybe we could be
more than just scary villains.

00:06:43.026 --> 00:06:44.026
[gasps]

00:06:45.404 --> 00:06:46.404
What...

00:06:46.488 --> 00:06:47.655
[Tarantula] Oh, wow!

00:06:47.739 --> 00:06:49.782
Is this... Is this "wagging"?

00:06:51.785 --> 00:06:53.411
[Tarantula] We're wagging!

00:06:55.205 --> 00:06:57.832
No! No! No!

00:06:57.916 --> 00:07:01.836
We'll always be bad guys!

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:09.594
[panting]

00:07:24.985 --> 00:07:27.987
[cackling]

00:07:28.071 --> 00:07:30.490
Faster, faster, my little pigs.

00:07:30.574 --> 00:07:32.283
[children cheering]

00:07:35.287 --> 00:07:37.205
- [thudding]
- [tires screeching]

00:07:37.873 --> 00:07:38.706
[all gasping]

00:07:39.583 --> 00:07:40.708
[chitters]

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:42.502
[screams]

00:07:42.586 --> 00:07:43.586
No!

00:07:47.299 --> 00:07:48.549
[cackling]

00:07:51.887 --> 00:07:53.471
[driver screams]

00:07:57.935 --> 00:08:00.269
[all screaming]

00:08:00.354 --> 00:08:02.146
[chittering]

00:08:04.858 --> 00:08:07.818
[people screaming]

00:08:12.741 --> 00:08:13.783
[tires screeching]

00:08:15.327 --> 00:08:17.912
Once we steal the meteorite,
we take it straight to the police.

00:08:17.996 --> 00:08:19.830
And all will be forgiven.

00:08:19.915 --> 00:08:23.376
I don't know about "all,"
but it's a start.

